# Normalize line endings: store LF in the repo, check out native.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep shell + python LF even on Windows checkouts.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Markdown/JSON are text.
*.md text
*.json text

# The committed code graph is a SQLite file. Marking it binary stops git from
# mangling it with eol conversion and stops it flooding a diff — git's packfile
# delta still compresses it across refreshes, so history stays small.
#
# `diff=codegraph` makes it reviewable anyway: with the driver configured, git
# renders the graph as its JSON export, so `git diff` / `show` / `log -p` show
# which nodes changed instead of "Binary files differ". Without the driver
# nothing breaks — git falls back to treating it as opaque. Configure with:
#     /codebase-kg:setup-diff        (or see docs/REVIEW.md)
*.db binary diff=codegraph
code_graph.db binary diff=codegraph
